## Naming Convention

- Folder names: `NN_descriptive_name` (zero-padded number prefix for ordering).
- File names: `snake_case` matching the folder purpose.
- Each folder contains exactly one `.md` and one `.tex` file (plus optional images in `assets/`).

## Content Standards

### Markdown Files
- Use ATX-style headings (`#`, `##`, `###`).
- Use fenced code blocks with language tags.
- Include a YAML front-matter block with title, date, level, and author.
- Tables use GitHub Flavored Markdown pipe syntax.

### LaTeX Files
- Use `\documentclass{article}` with `12pt, a4paper`.
- Standard packages: `hyperref`, `listings`, `graphicx`, `booktabs`, `geometry`.
- Listings for code blocks with appropriate language highlighting.
- Match the heading hierarchy to the Markdown version.

## When to Update Documentation

- After completing any level milestone.
- After adding new scraping sources or ETL pipelines.
- After modifying architecture or deployment topology.
- After any prompt engineering session (update prompts_log).
